;; The sha is the RATCHET: coverage floors measured against one loader do
;; not carry to another, so changing tools/kexe_loader.c must fail here
;; until someone decides what the floors are for the new one.
;;
;; Advanced 2026-09-09 for the granted-region argument forms (`g:<hex>`
;; and `gl:<n>`), the report tail, and the pool-is-last assert.
;;
;; ⚠ THE FLOORS BELOW WERE NOT RE-MEASURED. They are the previous
;; loader's, carried forward, and that is stated rather than implied:
;; libFuzzer's runtime (libclang_rt.fuzzer_osx.a) is not installed on
;; the machine that made this change, so `npm run fuzz` there takes the
;; deterministic-sanitized arm and never reaches this file. The Linux CI
;; job is what measures them. The change ADDS parser branches rather
;; than removing any, so the floors should be met or exceeded -- but
;; "should" is the word, and if CI reports higher numbers these floors
;; are now looser than the code deserves and should be raised.
;;
;; Advanced 2026-09-10 for arena_exhausted: the parser is untouched, so this
;; is the ratchet doing its bookkeeping rather than reporting a new surface.
;; The floors are again NOT re-measured, for the same reason as above, and
;; the change adds no parser branch at all -- the new code runs only on
;; paths that were already about to raise(SIGILL).
